  "body": "## Problem\n\nOn Windows, agents commit some files with CRLF line endings, while `main` uses LF. In PR #3790, 10 files came in with CRLF. A 5-line change in `generate.rs` showed as about 4500 changed lines, and the churn caused two of three merge conflicts. PR #3737 had the same problem with two files.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Add a `.gitattributes` at the repository root with `* text=auto eol=lf`. Add explicit `binary` rules for PNG, STEP, STL and other binary fixtures, so that Git never changes them.\n- Do not renormalize the whole tree in the same PR. If files on `main` have CRLF now, list them and normalize them in one separate commit.\n- Check that the snapshot PNGs, `tests/golden/*`, `.cl` and `.cnc` fixtures are not changed by the rule.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Found by the review of PR #3790.\n- `.gitattributes` is not a process file. The PR needs a normal review.\n",
